.TH BIFROST 1 2000-1月 "as.gff3" "as.gff3"
.SH NAME
as.gff3 \- cast the gene prediction result as GFF3 table format
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIas.gff3(\fBx\fR as any, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
cast the gene prediction result as GFF3 table format
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBx\fB \fR\- 
 the gene prediction result, which can be the output of "prodigal" function, or a pipeline that produces PredictionResult objects. The pipeline can be created by using the "pipeline" function in R#, and the final output of the pipeline should be PredictionResult objects. For example, if you have a pipeline that produces PredictionResult objects, you can pass it directly to this function to get the GFF3 table format output.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Annotation.Assembly.NCBI.GenBank.TabularFormat.GFF.GFFTable\fR object that contains all of the predicted genes 
 as the \fBCDS\fR feature, the score of each feature is the total score of 
 the corresponding predicted gene, and the score details are stored in the 
 attributes of the feature, example as \fBstart_codon\fR, \fBrbs_motif\fR, 
 \fBcscore\fR, \fBsscore\fR, \fBrscore\fR, \fBtscore\fR, \fBuscore\fR and 
 \fBpartial\fR.
 
 this function returns a R# error message object if the input data can not 
 be cast to a collection of the @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Annotation.Prodigal.PredictionResult\fR object.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
bifrost
.SH FILES
.PP
seqtoolkit.dll
.PP
